1
00:00:00,270 --> 00:00:01,540
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,540 --> 00:00:03,310
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,310 --> 00:00:05,080
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:12,150
(10 years ago)

5
00:00:13,490 --> 00:00:14,850
(Episode 45)

6
00:00:25,230 --> 00:00:27,300
Are you Ko Eun Seol?

7
00:00:33,810 --> 00:00:36,570
Sympathy
or a sense of responsibility.

8
00:00:37,310 --> 00:00:40,040
Somewhere in between,
that's what I thought at first.

9
00:00:43,150 --> 00:00:45,450
Objection.

10
00:00:46,220 --> 00:00:47,220
Witness.

11
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:49,250
Then why is your testimony different
from your report?

12
00:00:49,350 --> 00:00:50,790
You were my very first client,

13
00:00:52,090 --> 00:00:53,790
and firsts are always special.

14
00:00:55,130 --> 00:00:56,760
That's why I thought
I was helping you.

15
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:04,700
Eun Seol, are you okay?

16
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:06,470
To you, I was only Team Leader Seo.

17
00:01:07,310 --> 00:01:08,540
I was just a lawyer to you.

18
00:01:09,770 --> 00:01:10,780
I was...

19
00:01:11,280 --> 00:01:12,540
just your Daddy Long Legs.

20
00:01:13,580 --> 00:01:14,850
It's not that bad.

21
00:01:15,210 --> 00:01:16,480
Eun Seol,

22
00:01:17,420 --> 00:01:19,680
I kept telling myself
that's all I ever was to you.

23
00:01:25,620 --> 00:01:26,620
Eun Seol,

24
00:01:27,860 --> 00:01:29,790
who am I to you?

25
00:01:33,060 --> 00:01:34,200
Not as your lawyer,

26
00:01:35,700 --> 00:01:37,700
but as your man.

27
00:01:40,210 --> 00:01:41,210
I...

28
00:01:42,010 --> 00:01:45,580
I haven't really
thought about you that way.

29
00:01:46,580 --> 00:01:47,710
Gosh, my bad.

30
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:54,050
But no matter
how often I reminded myself,

31
00:01:55,990 --> 00:01:58,660
I couldn't suppress
what I was feeling.

32
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:00,260
(Design Team)

33
00:02:08,130 --> 00:02:09,170
Right up to the end,

34
00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:12,840
I wanted to stay by your side
and help you,

35
00:02:14,670 --> 00:02:16,740
but I ended up failing
as your Daddy Long Legs.

36
00:02:18,810 --> 00:02:20,710
I'm sorry, Eun Seol.

37
00:02:36,730 --> 00:02:37,730
Team Leader Seo.

38
00:02:39,330 --> 00:02:40,470
They say...

39
00:02:41,970 --> 00:02:43,800
people who are too nosy...

40
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:47,570
have short lives.

41
00:02:49,210 --> 00:02:52,780
You should've lived
a little more selfishly.

42
00:02:55,850 --> 00:02:57,350
When you get to the afterlife,

43
00:02:57,980 --> 00:03:00,120
rest in peace.

44
00:03:50,940 --> 00:03:51,970
Ae Sook.

45
00:03:52,770 --> 00:03:53,770
Joo Ae Sook.

46
00:03:56,110 --> 00:03:57,780
Are you sure about this?

47
00:04:13,290 --> 00:04:14,630
I told you already.

48
00:04:16,030 --> 00:04:18,130
My name is Joo Mi Ran.

49
00:04:20,770 --> 00:04:23,800
A pathetic loser like you
no longer exists.

50
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:27,210
Can you truly bear...

51
00:04:28,540 --> 00:04:30,270
the weight of this sin?

52
00:04:33,310 --> 00:04:34,310
Sin?

53
00:04:35,250 --> 00:04:36,250
What sin?

54
00:04:37,380 --> 00:04:39,420
Kim Jung Sun is the one
who should pay.

55
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:43,660
Because of that witch,
my soul died countless times.

56
00:04:48,160 --> 00:04:49,160
Now,

57
00:04:50,030 --> 00:04:52,060
I'm going back to where I belong.

58
00:05:34,710 --> 00:05:36,770
Last night at a warehouse
in Gyeonggi Province,

59
00:05:36,840 --> 00:05:38,980
a man in his 30s was found dead,

60
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:40,750
and the police have launched
an investigation.

61
00:05:41,080 --> 00:05:43,380
Police who responded to a call
from the warehouse manager...

62
00:05:43,450 --> 00:05:45,050
ran a fingerprint check,

63
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:48,950
confirming the victim
was corporate lawyer Mr. Seo.

64
00:05:49,350 --> 00:05:50,920
Since the crime scene is...

65
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:52,760
in a remote area
with minimal foot traffic...

66
00:05:52,790 --> 00:05:55,230
and no nearby security cameras,

67
00:05:55,230 --> 00:05:57,360
police are struggling...

68
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:59,960
to identify the suspect
and track their escape route.

69
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:28,790
What were the autopsy results again?

70
00:06:30,030 --> 00:06:31,260
The cause of death was revealed...

71
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:33,730
to be shock from severe blood loss.

72
00:06:34,630 --> 00:06:36,670
The results came out
faster than I thought.

73
00:06:38,570 --> 00:06:41,470
Did you say the funeral
was wrapped up today?

74
00:06:41,810 --> 00:06:44,310
Yes, that's what I heard.

75
00:06:44,810 --> 00:06:46,080
What can you do?

76
00:06:46,980 --> 00:06:49,010
This was the end of the line
for Team Leader Seo.

77
00:06:49,710 --> 00:06:52,050
Everyone's lifespan is already set,
isn't it?

78
00:06:53,620 --> 00:06:55,290
Even if it weren't for what you did,

79
00:06:55,950 --> 00:06:57,760
that was ultimately
Seo Hyun Jae's fate.

80
00:07:00,760 --> 00:07:03,860
Even so,
you should've been more careful.

81
00:07:04,530 --> 00:07:07,200
I definitely checked. He was just...

82
00:07:08,230 --> 00:07:09,930
He was only briefly knocked out.

83
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:12,200
And while there was some bleeding,

84
00:07:12,740 --> 00:07:15,170
it wasn't severe enough
to induce shock.

85
00:07:15,370 --> 00:07:16,910
My heart is heavy, too.

86
00:07:17,340 --> 00:07:19,410
But what can you do?
What's done is done.

87
00:07:20,180 --> 00:07:21,780
Just shake it off
as fast as you can.

88
00:07:22,450 --> 00:07:24,220
I'll take care of the aftermath.

89
00:07:24,980 --> 00:07:25,980
Ma'am.

90
00:07:27,890 --> 00:07:28,890
Will I really...

91
00:07:29,650 --> 00:07:30,690
be okay?

92
00:07:32,890 --> 00:07:33,960
Of course.

93
00:07:34,790 --> 00:07:36,190
Just trust me, Secretary Choi.

94
00:07:49,710 --> 00:07:51,340
(Head of Legal Affairs)

95
00:08:09,330 --> 00:08:11,030
Still, if things ever get tough,
let me know.

96
00:08:12,160 --> 00:08:13,500
I guess I should show you.

97
00:08:14,500 --> 00:08:16,770
You know my legs
are super long, right?

98
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:21,470
I'm on call 24 hours a day,

99
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:23,910
so call your Daddy Long Legs
anytime.

100
00:08:48,570 --> 00:08:50,000
Mom, what's with the abalone?

101
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:51,270
This?

102
00:08:51,540 --> 00:08:53,600
There's nothing better
when you have no energy.

103
00:08:53,940 --> 00:08:57,410
I hope she eats this
and gets her strength back quickly.

104
00:08:57,780 --> 00:08:58,840
Wait.

105
00:08:59,110 --> 00:09:00,610
Is this for Teun Teun's Mom?

106
00:09:00,810 --> 00:09:01,810
Yes.

107
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:06,780
How long can she sit in despair
when she has a child to care for?

108
00:09:07,080 --> 00:09:08,420
The living must go on living.

109
00:09:08,620 --> 00:09:09,650
Right.

110
00:09:10,050 --> 00:09:11,160
I remember...

111
00:09:11,520 --> 00:09:13,890
when I had to let my wife go.

112
00:09:14,390 --> 00:09:17,130
I ate the abalone porridge you made
and got my strength back.

113
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:20,970
I have to admit,
you make a mean abalone porridge.

114
00:09:21,170 --> 00:09:22,470
Wait. Hold on.

115
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:25,240
When this porridge is done,
you take it to her.

116
00:09:25,300 --> 00:09:27,710
Why?
I mean, Eun Guk can give it to her.

117
00:09:27,740 --> 00:09:31,240
What if my eldest grandson
ends up filling her empty heart?

118
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:33,440
When someone is lonely,

119
00:09:33,780 --> 00:09:36,180
they can catch feelings
that weren't there before.

120
00:09:36,350 --> 00:09:38,680
You really can't help yourself,
can you?

121
00:09:38,720 --> 00:09:42,490
What's so bad about Eun Guk
comforting her lonely heart?

122
00:09:42,790 --> 00:09:45,620
As long as she finds comfort somehow,
it's a good thing.

123
00:09:46,090 --> 00:09:47,260
You said it yourself.

124
00:09:47,660 --> 00:09:49,560
The living must go on living.

125
00:09:49,760 --> 00:09:50,760
Even so,

126
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:53,900
it could never be our Eun Guk.
Not a chance.

127
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:55,430
The nerve.

128
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:38,340
Also, square your shoulders
like this.

129
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:40,280
Come on. What are you worried about?

130
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:43,580
You've got a reliable lawyer
for a brother right by your side.

131
00:10:44,580 --> 00:10:46,550
So don't be intimidated.

132
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:49,150
I'll take care of everything.

133
00:11:13,210 --> 00:11:14,210
Eun Seol.

134
00:11:28,190 --> 00:11:29,230
Attorney Seo.

135
00:11:32,060 --> 00:11:33,260
Attorney Seo.

136
00:11:35,830 --> 00:11:36,900
Attorney Seo.

137
00:11:45,780 --> 00:11:47,380
You knew, didn't you?

138
00:11:48,050 --> 00:11:49,310
You knew it'd turn out like this.

139
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:51,680
No.

140
00:11:54,290 --> 00:11:55,350
I...

141
00:11:56,290 --> 00:11:58,590
I'll find the real killer,
get my revenge,

142
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:02,090
and return to how things used to be.

143
00:12:03,930 --> 00:12:05,100
Deep down, you know.

144
00:12:06,030 --> 00:12:08,230
Even if you get revenge
and find the truth,

145
00:12:09,270 --> 00:12:12,270
you can never go back
to the normal life you had.

146
00:12:14,170 --> 00:12:15,270
No...

147
00:12:17,110 --> 00:12:18,210
No...

148
00:12:18,810 --> 00:12:21,650
No...

149
00:12:22,980 --> 00:12:25,320
- No...
- Keep being stubborn like that.

150
00:12:33,690 --> 00:12:35,430
I wonder who will die next.

151
00:12:45,400 --> 00:12:46,470
No...

152
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:48,470
No...

153
00:12:49,410 --> 00:12:50,570
No...

154
00:12:59,480 --> 00:13:02,990
Why do these unfortunate incidents
keep happening at the company?

155
00:13:03,490 --> 00:13:05,560
You heard about Team Leader Seo
in Legal, right?

156
00:13:07,530 --> 00:13:08,730
Yes, I heard.

157
00:13:09,130 --> 00:13:11,300
A random thug did that to him.

158
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:14,400
That appears to be
what the police concluded.

159
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:16,230
I saw on the news...

160
00:13:16,400 --> 00:13:18,400
that random, unprovoked assaults
like back in the '80s are...

161
00:13:18,770 --> 00:13:20,300
on the rise again.

162
00:13:20,300 --> 00:13:22,070
I'm not all that surprised.

163
00:13:22,070 --> 00:13:25,010
People's tempers have gotten
way more explosive lately.

164
00:13:25,040 --> 00:13:26,540
That said,

165
00:13:27,040 --> 00:13:30,110
isn't there something we can do
to boost staff morale?

166
00:13:30,180 --> 00:13:32,050
Like safety training, for instance.

167
00:13:33,420 --> 00:13:34,790
Do you think providing
that kind of training...

168
00:13:34,850 --> 00:13:36,790
would actually be effective?

169
00:13:37,720 --> 00:13:40,520
Everyone should handle
their own safety.

170
00:13:40,790 --> 00:13:43,130
Does the company really need
to offer that kind of training?

171
00:13:43,490 --> 00:13:45,460
It's not like this is a school.

172
00:13:45,560 --> 00:13:47,230
It's not merely about training.

173
00:13:47,300 --> 00:13:50,500
It's intended to soothe
our shaken employees.

174
00:13:50,530 --> 00:13:55,010
Do we have the luxury to sit around
tending to our employees' feelings?

175
00:13:55,040 --> 00:13:57,640
The quarterly performance report
is right around the corner.

176
00:13:59,340 --> 00:14:02,710
Sometimes it seems like
you mistake running this company...

177
00:14:03,010 --> 00:14:05,420
for a public service.

178
00:14:08,890 --> 00:14:09,990
Ma'am,

179
00:14:10,490 --> 00:14:13,190
what should we do about dinner
with the directors tomorrow?

180
00:14:14,630 --> 00:14:16,130
My husband will be busy,

181
00:14:16,190 --> 00:14:18,760
so we'll just keep it simple
with the board members.

182
00:14:19,030 --> 00:14:21,400
You made plans too?

183
00:14:21,470 --> 00:14:22,530
Yes.

184
00:14:23,300 --> 00:14:24,500
You did too?

185
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:25,670
Yes.

186
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:29,240
I made these plans
one month in advance.

187
00:14:29,970 --> 00:14:31,680
I wanted to take care
of the foundation's board members...

188
00:14:31,680 --> 00:14:32,880
before the general assembly.

189
00:14:33,410 --> 00:14:35,880
Then you should've told me
beforehand.

190
00:14:36,780 --> 00:14:39,080
You should've let me know first.

191
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:40,150
Like I said,

192
00:14:40,220 --> 00:14:42,250
I set up this appointment
a month ago.

193
00:14:47,890 --> 00:14:49,860
Should I cancel the appointment
with the directors?

194
00:14:50,460 --> 00:14:54,270
No, why should we?
Proceed as planned.

195
00:14:55,370 --> 00:14:58,800
If we do that,
the directors will be confused.

196
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:02,510
My husband likely
won't cancel either.

197
00:15:03,410 --> 00:15:07,410
This will be a great chance to see
which side the directors are on.

198
00:15:08,180 --> 00:15:11,150
It's up to the directors to choose,
so let's just observe.

199
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:14,590
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation)

200
00:15:14,590 --> 00:15:17,220
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

201
00:15:22,730 --> 00:15:23,790
Director Hong, hello.

202
00:15:25,060 --> 00:15:26,960
Shouldn't we meet up?

203
00:15:28,430 --> 00:15:31,570
Yes. How about lunch
with the directors?

204
00:15:33,370 --> 00:15:34,370
Ko Eun Seol,

205
00:15:34,940 --> 00:15:36,770
did you look into
the engagement ring designs?

206
00:15:42,550 --> 00:15:45,020
I categorized
and organized them by brand.

207
00:15:49,390 --> 00:15:50,390
Well...

208
00:15:51,420 --> 00:15:52,720
I've already seen all of these.

209
00:15:53,490 --> 00:15:54,690
Good job, though.

210
00:15:56,160 --> 00:15:57,160
Ko Eun Seol.

211
00:15:57,590 --> 00:15:59,860
When are you free?

212
00:16:02,170 --> 00:16:03,870
We have to pick out
the ring together.

213
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:05,940
I need to schedule our ring tour.

214
00:16:06,870 --> 00:16:08,470
Do I have to go with you?

215
00:16:08,510 --> 00:16:09,870
Of course.

216
00:16:10,070 --> 00:16:11,410
You worked hard to pick these out,

217
00:16:11,480 --> 00:16:12,810
so what's the point
if you don't come with me?

218
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:15,010
I told you.

219
00:16:15,310 --> 00:16:18,080
Your sense of taste is
so remarkable...

220
00:16:18,320 --> 00:16:19,580
that I want your input.

221
00:16:20,950 --> 00:16:22,890
That sounds like coercion,
not a request.

222
00:16:23,920 --> 00:16:27,090
If you need my help,
you should ask politely.

223
00:16:28,230 --> 00:16:29,230
What?

224
00:16:29,860 --> 00:16:30,960
I should ask you?

225
00:16:32,460 --> 00:16:34,970
Yes. Help is supposed
to be requested,

226
00:16:35,700 --> 00:16:36,830
not commanded.

227
00:16:38,140 --> 00:16:40,170
Besides, it's your engagement.

228
00:16:40,570 --> 00:16:42,210
If you really need my help,

229
00:16:42,370 --> 00:16:45,240
Chief Cha should ask me as well.

230
00:16:45,480 --> 00:16:46,580
Seok Jin too?

231
00:16:47,080 --> 00:16:49,410
If the two of you ask me sincerely,

232
00:16:50,210 --> 00:16:51,880
I'll think about it then.

233
00:16:52,350 --> 00:16:54,050
Whether to join the ring tour
or not.

234
00:17:01,330 --> 00:17:02,330
You're here early.

235
00:17:03,590 --> 00:17:07,060
Yes, Auntie dropped me off early.

236
00:17:09,870 --> 00:17:12,140
Why do you always carry that around?

237
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:15,610
Oh, this?

238
00:17:15,670 --> 00:17:19,210
Coloring makes me feel at peace.

239
00:17:21,850 --> 00:17:24,250
Hae Ra, do you want to try?

240
00:17:25,150 --> 00:17:26,220
Forget it.

241
00:17:26,680 --> 00:17:30,290
Come on. Did you really
have to knock it away?

242
00:17:33,960 --> 00:17:34,990
I...

243
00:17:35,430 --> 00:17:37,530
didn't meet up with you
to draw stuff like this.

244
00:17:42,970 --> 00:17:43,970
Ms. Park.

245
00:17:44,500 --> 00:17:47,740
Are you really that against
Seok Jin and me getting engaged?

246
00:17:48,670 --> 00:17:50,540
Yes, I hate it.

247
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:53,140
Why? Why do you hate it?

248
00:17:55,010 --> 00:17:57,980
You always yell at me
whenever you see me.

249
00:17:58,550 --> 00:17:59,620
That's why.

250
00:18:04,050 --> 00:18:06,420
You keep pushing my buttons,

251
00:18:06,490 --> 00:18:08,060
so I keep losing my temper.

252
00:18:09,090 --> 00:18:11,160
But that only makes you
hate me even more.

253
00:18:11,300 --> 00:18:13,230
Yes, exactly. That's it.

254
00:18:17,800 --> 00:18:21,910
Ms. Park, you must want
Seok Jin to be happy.

255
00:18:22,170 --> 00:18:23,410
Of course.

256
00:18:23,740 --> 00:18:26,280
For him to be happy,
he has to get engaged to me.

257
00:18:27,140 --> 00:18:28,180
He's someone...

258
00:18:28,810 --> 00:18:30,650
who can only be happy
if he's wealthy.

259
00:18:30,950 --> 00:18:32,950
I can make that happen.

260
00:18:36,090 --> 00:18:38,360
Do you have a lot of money, Hae Ra?

261
00:18:38,520 --> 00:18:41,390
Of course I do.
I have a ton of money.

262
00:18:43,330 --> 00:18:45,960
Can you make Seok Jin rich?

263
00:18:47,400 --> 00:18:49,370
- No.
- You can't.

264
00:18:50,230 --> 00:18:52,640
You can't make Seok Jin happy.

265
00:18:58,710 --> 00:18:59,710
Then...

266
00:19:02,280 --> 00:19:03,480
Hae Ra, you should...

267
00:19:06,880 --> 00:19:08,650
get engaged to Seok Jin.

268
00:19:10,050 --> 00:19:12,120
Now you're making sense.

269
00:19:13,260 --> 00:19:14,890
Go tell Seok Jin.

270
00:19:15,130 --> 00:19:16,860
Tell him
he has to get engaged to me.

271
00:19:17,190 --> 00:19:18,500
Say you gave us your blessing.

272
00:19:19,430 --> 00:19:20,430
Got it?

273
00:19:23,500 --> 00:19:24,740
I asked if you got it.

274
00:19:26,370 --> 00:19:27,440
Got it.

275
00:19:28,110 --> 00:19:30,170
And enough
with all this coloring and drawing.

276
00:19:30,240 --> 00:19:32,280
You're not a kid, so grow up.

277
00:19:35,150 --> 00:19:36,180
Hold on.

278
00:19:41,050 --> 00:19:44,660
Hae Ra, you might be able
to make Seok Jin rich,

279
00:19:46,260 --> 00:19:47,460
but don't you actually love him?

280
00:19:50,130 --> 00:19:51,660
Engagement and marriage...

281
00:19:51,800 --> 00:19:54,260
are meant for people
who actually love each other.

282
00:20:01,310 --> 00:20:02,670
Of course I love him.

283
00:20:30,070 --> 00:20:33,540
Directors, thank you so much
for taking the time to be here.

284
00:20:33,540 --> 00:20:35,070
Please don't mention it.

285
00:20:36,710 --> 00:20:39,010
- Please enjoy the food.
- Yes, thank you for the meal.

286
00:20:39,010 --> 00:20:41,180
- We'll enjoy the meal.
- It looks delicious.

287
00:20:47,150 --> 00:20:49,690
- Well then, let's eat.
- Sure.

288
00:20:50,620 --> 00:20:52,220
- I'll enjoy.
- Let's dig in.

289
00:21:24,350 --> 00:21:25,420
Director Joo.

290
00:21:27,260 --> 00:21:28,530
Did you wait long?

291
00:21:33,960 --> 00:21:38,300
Are you sure every single director
has sided with her?

292
00:21:39,470 --> 00:21:40,470
Yes.

293
00:21:40,740 --> 00:21:42,170
They're having dinner right now...

294
00:21:42,510 --> 00:21:45,440
discussing everything
right up to next year's budget.

295
00:21:47,640 --> 00:21:50,810
Is she trying this hard
just to beat me?

296
00:21:52,280 --> 00:21:54,280
Since it was
the Chairman's invitation,

297
00:21:54,280 --> 00:21:56,090
they likely scrambled
to get there...

298
00:21:57,290 --> 00:22:00,690
all trying to snag
one more benefit for themselves.

299
00:22:02,530 --> 00:22:04,360
You haven't eaten yet, right?

300
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:07,100
I haven't.

301
00:22:07,660 --> 00:22:08,670
Have a seat.

302
00:22:24,850 --> 00:22:27,750
- Are you asleep, Mom?
- You're home, Mr. Seok Jin.

303
00:22:28,620 --> 00:22:29,650
What are you doing up?

304
00:22:29,920 --> 00:22:32,060
Well, this got wrinkled,

305
00:22:32,190 --> 00:22:33,960
so I was going to smooth it out
before sleeping.

306
00:22:35,890 --> 00:22:37,760
Did you already color this much?

307
00:22:37,990 --> 00:22:39,460
You worked really hard on it.

308
00:22:39,600 --> 00:22:41,800
The nice lady gave it to me,

309
00:22:41,930 --> 00:22:43,730
so I worked even harder on it.

310
00:22:46,040 --> 00:22:48,110
Get ready for bed.
I'll go change my clothes.

311
00:22:50,240 --> 00:22:51,510
Mr. Seok Jin.

312
00:22:54,750 --> 00:22:55,850
Just get engaged...

313
00:22:56,980 --> 00:22:59,150
to Hae Ra.

314
00:22:59,820 --> 00:23:00,880
What did you say?

315
00:23:01,990 --> 00:23:03,720
Why did you suddenly
change your mind?

316
00:23:04,020 --> 00:23:05,260
You know,

317
00:23:05,790 --> 00:23:08,590
I just want you to be happy.

318
00:23:10,230 --> 00:23:11,760
Hae Ra told me...

319
00:23:12,500 --> 00:23:15,230
that she can make you happy.

320
00:23:17,730 --> 00:23:20,840
Then, I'm completely fine with it.

321
00:23:22,640 --> 00:23:26,110
So please get engaged to Hae Ra.

322
00:23:29,250 --> 00:23:31,620
Are you really okay with that?

323
00:23:36,890 --> 00:23:38,490
You don't have to force yourself.

324
00:23:39,320 --> 00:23:43,330
Mom, let's take a little time
and think this through slowly.

325
00:23:44,490 --> 00:23:47,160
What if Hae Ra gets angry
while we take our time?

326
00:23:47,860 --> 00:23:48,970
So,

327
00:23:49,600 --> 00:23:50,630
Seok Jin,

328
00:23:51,030 --> 00:23:53,000
you must get engaged to Hae Ra.

329
00:23:53,740 --> 00:23:54,740
Okay?

330
00:23:58,380 --> 00:24:00,580
You have no idea
how shocked I was...

331
00:24:01,140 --> 00:24:03,080
to hear about Team Leader Seo.

332
00:24:03,610 --> 00:24:05,320
I only found out
through the news as well.

333
00:24:08,250 --> 00:24:09,350
By any chance,

334
00:24:09,550 --> 00:24:11,090
did Team Leader Seo...

335
00:24:11,090 --> 00:24:14,090
say anything specific to you
before the incident?

336
00:24:15,760 --> 00:24:18,260
No, he didn't.

337
00:24:18,860 --> 00:24:21,400
He cared about you a lot,

338
00:24:21,870 --> 00:24:22,900
so I was curious...

339
00:24:22,900 --> 00:24:25,200
if he said something to you
before it happened.

340
00:24:26,600 --> 00:24:29,370
You relied on him a lot too, right?

341
00:24:30,410 --> 00:24:31,410
Yes.

342
00:24:32,110 --> 00:24:34,880
He was like a big brother to me.

343
00:24:36,510 --> 00:24:37,680
I see.

344
00:24:38,780 --> 00:24:40,120
It's so tragic.

345
00:24:40,880 --> 00:24:41,890
That's why...

346
00:24:43,650 --> 00:24:44,790
I'm determined...

347
00:24:45,490 --> 00:24:46,760
to uncover the truth.

348
00:24:51,290 --> 00:24:52,530
The day he died,

349
00:24:52,930 --> 00:24:54,970
he told me he had something to say.

350
00:24:56,230 --> 00:24:57,230
Is that so?

351
00:24:58,000 --> 00:25:00,200
But you don't know
what it was about?

352
00:25:00,370 --> 00:25:01,370
I don't.

353
00:25:02,470 --> 00:25:04,910
Whatever he was trying to tell me,

354
00:25:06,540 --> 00:25:08,810
and whoever did this to him...

355
00:25:11,210 --> 00:25:12,820
I'm going to find out.

356
00:25:14,990 --> 00:25:16,050
But what if...

357
00:25:16,690 --> 00:25:19,520
you end up putting yourself
in danger, too?

358
00:25:20,460 --> 00:25:21,490
Are you sure about this?

359
00:25:21,730 --> 00:25:22,730
Yes.

360
00:25:23,730 --> 00:25:25,360
I have nothing left to lose.

361
00:25:27,700 --> 00:25:29,130
I'll be rooting for you.

362
00:25:43,310 --> 00:25:44,310
All right.

363
00:25:44,310 --> 00:25:46,620
I just assumed
that you had feelings for him too.

364
00:25:46,980 --> 00:25:48,650
I told you I don't,

365
00:25:48,650 --> 00:25:50,850
so why do you keep pushing me
and getting on my nerves?

366
00:25:50,850 --> 00:25:52,360
I said I don't!

367
00:25:54,020 --> 00:25:55,230
Don't you believe me either?

368
00:25:55,990 --> 00:25:59,300
Of course I believe you.
All right, I was wrong.

369
00:25:59,530 --> 00:26:01,030
I completely misunderstood.

370
00:26:01,030 --> 00:26:04,200
Don't make assumptions about me
just because I'm a single mom.

371
00:26:04,430 --> 00:26:06,670
Do you think I'm easy enough
to fall for just any man?

372
00:26:08,640 --> 00:26:09,640
I'm sorry, Mi Rae.

373
00:26:09,710 --> 00:26:12,340
Forget it.
You're just like everyone else.

374
00:26:13,410 --> 00:26:14,410
Mi Rae...

375
00:26:30,660 --> 00:26:31,660
Boss.

376
00:26:32,300 --> 00:26:33,600
Did you finish mopping the floor?

377
00:26:34,200 --> 00:26:35,370
Yes, I finished mopping.

378
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:38,670
I'll clean up the rest,
so you should go home.

379
00:26:42,470 --> 00:26:44,040
You should go home and rest.

380
00:26:44,470 --> 00:26:45,740
You still don't look well,

381
00:26:46,080 --> 00:26:48,080
and it'll be a disaster
if you collapse too.

382
00:26:48,210 --> 00:26:49,210
Just let me be.

383
00:26:49,280 --> 00:26:52,150
If I don't do at least this,
I might lose my mind!

384
00:26:58,960 --> 00:27:00,160
Lean on me.

385
00:27:00,790 --> 00:27:01,790
It's okay to do that right now.

386
00:27:01,790 --> 00:27:04,790
Do you even know whose fault it is
that I snapped at Hyun Jae?

387
00:27:05,130 --> 00:27:09,470
If it weren't for you, I would've
never yelled at Hyun Jae so coldly!

388
00:27:16,040 --> 00:27:18,810
Do you have any idea
how angry I got at him?

389
00:27:21,010 --> 00:27:24,250
I shouldn't have yelled
and lost my temper like that.

390
00:27:30,450 --> 00:27:31,450
If...

391
00:27:34,590 --> 00:27:36,890
Had I known
that would be our last moment...

392
00:27:38,560 --> 00:27:42,300
I would've just given him
a warm hug.

393
00:27:44,870 --> 00:27:46,300
You're right.
I'm so sorry for everything.

394
00:27:46,740 --> 00:27:48,510
If resenting me
helps you feel better,

395
00:27:48,770 --> 00:27:50,340
then resent me and blame me
all you like.

396
00:27:50,870 --> 00:27:52,110
I'm completely fine with that.

397
00:28:28,110 --> 00:28:29,110
Eun Seol.

398
00:28:37,490 --> 00:28:39,360
What kind of person
was Team Leader Seo?

399
00:28:42,660 --> 00:28:44,530
To me, Attorney Seo...

400
00:28:47,330 --> 00:28:49,100
was like a tree.

401
00:28:52,570 --> 00:28:54,970
Standing beneath a tree,
you don't really feel it.

402
00:28:56,240 --> 00:28:58,370
Whether the sun's scorching hot...

403
00:29:00,880 --> 00:29:02,910
or the rain's coming down hard.

404
00:29:09,790 --> 00:29:11,920
Beneath the shelter
that he provided,

405
00:29:15,790 --> 00:29:18,230
I didn't know
how precious that shade was.

406
00:29:26,070 --> 00:29:27,070
I'll never again...

407
00:29:31,940 --> 00:29:34,740
find someone
like the tree he was to me.

408
00:29:41,120 --> 00:29:42,190
Did Mr. Seo...

409
00:29:44,620 --> 00:29:46,290
mean that much to you?

410
00:29:47,460 --> 00:29:48,460
Yes.

411
00:29:51,760 --> 00:29:52,900
To the very end,

412
00:29:54,730 --> 00:29:56,770
he was my shade.

413
00:30:00,540 --> 00:30:02,110
I owe him so much,

414
00:30:07,340 --> 00:30:08,710
and I'm so grateful to him.

415
00:30:19,720 --> 00:30:20,960
I should get going.

416
00:30:21,490 --> 00:30:23,630
I'll take you home. Hold on.

417
00:30:23,630 --> 00:30:25,160
No, it's fine.

418
00:30:46,820 --> 00:30:47,880
Hyun Jae.

419
00:30:52,420 --> 00:30:53,420
Hey, no way.

420
00:30:54,020 --> 00:30:55,630
- It's been a while.
- Good to see you.

421
00:30:55,630 --> 00:30:57,160
- Where are you headed?
- Home.

422
00:30:57,160 --> 00:30:59,200
- Really?
- Have you had dinner?

423
00:31:30,430 --> 00:31:33,260
The person you are trying to reach
is unavailable.

424
00:31:33,260 --> 00:31:35,770
Please leave a message
after the tone.

425
00:31:58,960 --> 00:32:00,720
Seriously, Attorney Seo?

426
00:32:05,360 --> 00:32:07,360
Why aren't you answering my calls?

427
00:32:13,270 --> 00:32:16,710
You said you were on call
round the clock for free.

428
00:32:22,580 --> 00:32:24,680
Isn't this a clear neglect of duty?

429
00:32:29,090 --> 00:32:31,920
What kind of Daddy Long Legs
behaves like this?

430
00:33:01,320 --> 00:33:02,420
Attorney Seo.

431
00:33:04,650 --> 00:33:06,690
I will uncover the truth,
no matter what.

432
00:33:10,460 --> 00:33:12,560
Even the injustice
surrounding your death...

433
00:33:13,800 --> 00:33:15,470
I will uncover it all.

434
00:33:20,370 --> 00:33:21,770
So just trust me.

435
00:33:25,140 --> 00:33:27,280
Just like how I trusted
only you, Attorney Seo.

436
00:33:52,100 --> 00:33:55,840
(A Trap Called Desire)

437
00:33:55,940 --> 00:33:58,340
The engagement will take place
within the month.

438
00:33:58,340 --> 00:34:00,940
If you delay it any further,
we'll call the whole thing off.

439
00:34:00,940 --> 00:34:04,450
Having him institutionalized
at the right time seems cleanest.

440
00:34:04,750 --> 00:34:08,620
Had my daughter grown up safely,
she'd be exactly this age.

441
00:34:08,790 --> 00:34:12,360
Attorney Seo, what on earth
were you looking for?

442
00:34:12,690 --> 00:34:14,560
I'm on my way to the warehouse
where he died.

443
00:34:14,560 --> 00:34:16,560
There could be CCTV nearby
that the police missed.

444
00:34:16,560 --> 00:34:19,400
Then you two must've had dinner
alone that night.

445
00:34:19,400 --> 00:34:21,160
Did you mention that to me?

446
00:34:21,160 --> 00:34:22,730
I told you...

447
00:34:22,930 --> 00:34:25,130
not to be alone with my husband.

448
00:34:25,200 --> 00:34:27,800
What's his connection
to Chief Cha's father?

449
00:34:27,870 --> 00:34:29,010
I heard a man named Oh Tae Seop...

450
00:34:29,070 --> 00:34:31,870
was behind the accident
involving Chief Cha's father.

451
00:34:32,410 --> 00:34:34,410
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
